<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="2" type="enumerated">
  <item>A roll of paper that is 3 feet wide can be cut to any length.
  </item>
  <figure><media alt="Roll of paper, slightly unrolled. Its width is 3 feet."><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/add679acbffa6947a9d01c698c7e43b7c7bac3f7"/></media></figure></list>
<section class="check-understanding"><exercise data-content-id="d950e5f9-6c9d-4634-914a-7b1c2e36f47b" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>If we cut a length of 2.5 feet, what is the perimeter of the paper?
          
          
          Enter your answer in feet. <emphasis>Use integers only.</emphasis>
        </para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct! The perimeter of the paper is 11 feet. </para><para> Nice try! The correct answer is 11. The perimeter of the paper is 11 feet.</para></solution></exercise></section>

<para>For questions b-f, keep in mind that the roll of paper is 3 feet wide. Complete the table by answering each question.</para>

<table class="os-raise-midsizetable">
  <thead>
    <row>
      <entry><emphasis>
        side length (feet)
      </emphasis></entry><entry><emphasis>
        perimeter (feet)
      </emphasis></entry></row>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <row>
      <entry>
        <para>1</para>
      </entry>
      <entry>b. _______</entry>
    </row>
    <row>
      <entry>
        <para>2</para>
      </entry>
      <entry>c. _______</entry>
    </row>
    <row>
      <entry>
        <para>6.3</para>
      </entry>
      <entry>d. _______</entry>
    </row>
    <row>
      <entry>
        <para>11</para>
      </entry>
      <entry>f. _______</entry>
    </row>
  </tbody>
</table>


<section class="check-understanding"><exercise data-content-id="911a1006-037e-4c7a-945c-912d511b8773" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>If we cut a length of 1 foot, what is the perimeter of the paper to the nearest whole foot? 
          
          Enter your answer here:
        </para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct! The perimeter is 8 feet when the side length is \(1 cm\) \((1+3+1+3=8)\). </para><para> Nice try! The correct answer is 8. The perimeter is 8 feet when the side length is \(1 cm) \((1+3+1+3=8)\).</para></solution></exercise><exercise data-content-id="60456465-1eca-4c06-ab98-33262f38a76c" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>To the nearest whole foot, what is the perimeter when the side length is 2 feet?
          

          Enter your answer here:
        </para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct! The perimeter is 10 feet when the side length is \(2 cm\) \((2+3+2+3=10)\). </para><para> Nice try! The correct answer is 10. The perimeter is 10 feet when the side length is \(2 cm\) \((2+3+2+3=10)\).</para></solution></exercise><exercise data-content-id="ea0b7e59-c525-423d-9535-2e709157024e" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>What is the exact perimeter, in feet, when the side length is 6.3 feet?
          

          Enter your answer here:
        </para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct! The perimeter is 18.6 feet when the side length is \(6.3 cm\) \((6.3+3+6.3+3=18.6)\). </para><para> Nice try! The correct answer is 18.6. The perimeter is 18.6 feet when the side length is \(6.3 cm\) \((6.3+3+6.3+3=18.6)\).</para></solution></exercise><exercise data-content-id="eccf0aa0-7098-4211-a69a-d04113c0103d" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>What is the perimeter, to the nearest whole foot,when the side length is 11 feet?
          

          Enter your answer here:
        </para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct! The perimeter is 28 feet when the side length is \(11 cm\) \((11+3+11+3=28)\).
      </para><para> Nice try! The correct answer is 28. The perimeter is 28 feet when the side length is \(11 cm\) \((11+3+11+3=28)\).</para></solution></exercise></section>

<!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para>Write a rule for a function, P, that gives the perimeter of the paper in feet when the side length in feet is <emphasis>l</emphasis>.</para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:
    </para>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para>\(P(l)=6+2l\)</para>
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End -->


<!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para>What does P(11) represent in this situation? What is its value?</para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:
    </para>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para>\(P(11)\) is the perimeter of the paper in feet when the paper is cut at a length of 11 feet. Its value is 28.</para>
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End -->


